# Il2CppInterop reconstruction provenance.
# Consumed by scripts/build_il2cppinterop.sh.

UPSTREAM_URL=https://github.com/BepInEx/Il2CppInterop
# The ref the pin is compared against by scripts/check_upstream_pins.sh.
UPSTREAM_REF=master
UPSTREAM_COMMIT=81a6f78c8b653e0da4a3420ac4cd00819e8b6292
PATCH_FILE=references/il2cppinterop-arm64-disarm.patch

# The upstream HEAD does not handle Android ARM64 xrefs; the losses fork
# Il2CppInterop fork (Il2CppInterop restored source) adapted:
#   - Common/XrefScans: Iced x86 -> Disarm Arm64
#   - Runtime: module match == libil2cpp.so + NativeLibrary.Load("libil2cpp.so")
#   - Detour provider Create(..., specialReturnBuffer)
#   - Hook.ApplyHook: warn + non-fatal instead of throw
#   - All XrefScannerLowLevel call sites: 3-arg JumpTargets(x, ignoreRetn, instructions)
#   - x86 MemoryUtils signature scan branches removed from hook targeting
#   - Runtime + HarmonySupport retarget to net10.0
# Behaviour envelope keeps upstream HEAD explicit-version parts (GuardFix,
# Unity VersionHandler matrices) while preserving the fork's call-site hop
# distances that were tuned against real games.

DISARM_VERSION=2022.1.0-master.99
TFM_RUNTIME=net10.0
TFM_COMMON=netstandard2.0

# The compiler is pinned too, not just the sources. Upstream's global.json
# says SDK 8.0.0 with rollForward=latestMajor (relaxed from latestFeature by
# the patch above so the fork builds on a modern SDK), which resolves to the
# newest installed major — .NET 11 RC on a machine that has one, 10.0.401 on
# CI. Measured 2026-10-12: same tree, different compilers, no error anywhere.
# scripts/build_il2cppinterop.sh therefore rewrites the pin to the root
# global.json version for the duration of the build and restores it on exit,
# mirroring scripts/build_monomod.sh. The version is read from the root file,
# not duplicated here.

# Base-number policy: the base tracks the newest upstream tag at or before
# the pin (v1.5.3 here; the pin itself sits two commits past it), revised on
# pin bumps, never alone. A rename changes the assembly identity and needs a
# rebuild plus an on-device revalidation, so it always rides with real work.
# Distinct from upstream's own 1.5.3 so NuGet cannot silently reuse a remote
# package (or a stale global-cache entry) for our reference.
PACKAGE_VERSION=1.5.3-android.1
LOCAL_FEED=local-nuget
